__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Runtime logs from scheduled operational jobs (e.g. the launchd-run
# daily odds pull) -- pure noise, not provenance data worth preserving.
operational/logs/

# Reproducible/generated MoneyPuck research artifacts -- large binary/CSV
# blobs regenerable from the source download via
# research/moneypuck_ingestion/ingest_moneypuck_team.py. The raw files
# themselves are ignored, but the small .provenance.json sidecar
# manifests (filename, source URL, checksum, byte size, validation
# status) stay TRACKED, along with all ingestion code, schema, tests,
# and reports.
research/moneypuck_ingestion/raw/**/*.csv
research/moneypuck_ingestion/raw/**/*.zip
research/moneypuck_ingestion/research_moneypuck.db

# Same pattern for the goalie-intelligence raw MoneyPuck goalie
# game-by-game files (~11MB, reproducible via
# research/goalie_intelligence/build_starter_corpus.py) -- provenance.json
# and the normalized actual_starters.jsonl (the reviewed research
# corpus, analogous to research/real_nhl_results' own normalized file)
# stay tracked.
research/goalie_intelligence/raw/*.csv
research/player_sog/raw/*.csv
research/player_sog/player_game_sog.jsonl

# Same pattern for the blocked-shots and assists corpora -- both built
# from the SAME already-archived research/player_sog/raw/*.csv skater
# files (no separate download), reproducible via
# research/player_blocks/build_blocks_corpus.py and
# research/player_assists/build_assists_corpus.py.
research/player_blocks/player_game_blocks.jsonl
research/player_assists/player_game_assists.jsonl
research/player_points/player_game_points.jsonl
research/player_goals/player_game_goals.jsonl

# Secrets -- The Odds API key (research/live_sog_pricing/). Never commit.
# Raw captured live-odds JSON under data/raw/the_odds_api/ is intentionally
# NOT ignored -- small, genuine market observations worth preserving, same
# precedent as every other raw-provenance file in this project.
.env

# Daily operational MoneyPuck snapshot archive -- large, reproducible
# (re-downloadable via operational/moneypuck_daily.py, or reproducible
# from a manually-supplied local file), same pattern as every other raw
# MoneyPuck blob in this project. manifest.json sidecars (checksum,
# byte size, source URL, provenance_type) stay TRACKED.
data/raw/moneypuck/**/*.csv
data/raw/moneypuck/**/*.zip

# Local readiness snapshot -- regenerated by every `python3 sync_daily.py`
# run; not meaningful history to track.
operational/data_readiness_cache.json

# Live multi-market odds board cache -- regenerated by every
# operational/live_odds_daily_pull.py run, fully derivable from the
# TRACKED raw archive under data/raw/the_odds_api/live/; not meaningful
# history to track on its own.
operational/live_multimarket_board_cache.json

# Preseason Master Consolidation storage audit (PRESEASON_ENGINE_READINESS_
# REPORT.md Section AO): large, reproducible research artifacts that were
# untracked but not yet covered by .gitignore -- same regenerable-blob
# precedent as every other entry above, just added later than the slices
# that produced them.
research/real_nhl_pbp/research_pbp.db
research/real_nhl_pbp/raw/**/*.json
research/player_sog_period/player_game_period_sog.jsonl
research/joint_shot_workload/joint_shot_workload.jsonl
research/joint_scoring_dependence/joint_scoring.jsonl

# Prospective observation store (Preseason Operationalization sprint) --
# real operational data once the season starts, not a reproducible research
# artifact and not source code; back it up deliberately (operational/
# prospective_ledger.py::backup_db) rather than relying on git history.
operational/prospective_observations.db

# Paper bankroll store (Live DK / Paper Bankroll completion sprint,
# 2026-08-31) -- same reasoning: real accumulating operational data, not
# a reproducible research artifact, never committed.
operational/paper_bankroll.db

# Preseason Operational Readiness Closure sprint (2026-08-30): any future
# ad-hoc quarantine of confirmed-synthetic test pollution discovered under
# the real Odds API evidence tree (see tests/test_evidence_directory_
# isolation.py's regression guard, and the one-time cleanup this sprint
# already ran and deleted outright). Never applies to genuine captures.
data/raw/the_odds_api/**/_removed_test_fixture_pollution_*/

# Preseason Engine Freeze sprint (2026-08-30): found missing during this
# sprint's own repository checkpoint audit -- a real, 40MB regenerated
# SQLite research store (188,863 rows) built by the Live Special-Teams
# Role Shadow sprint, fully reproducible via
# `python3 -m operational.backfill_special_teams_history` from the
# already-ignored player_game_*.jsonl corpora. Same regenerable-blob
# precedent as research_pbp.db / research_moneypuck.db above.
operational/special_teams_history.db

# Same audit finding: two more regenerated derived research tables from
# the special-teams role sprints, neither previously ignored. The first
# (98MB) is reproducible via `python3 -m research.run_special_teams_role_transitions`;
# the second via `python3 -m research.build_team_game_special_teams_table`.
# Several later scripts (run_special_teams_role_overlay_sog.py and
# siblings) READ these as input -- see PRESEASON_FREEZE_MANIFEST.md's
# regeneration order before running them on a fresh clone.
research/special_teams_role_transitions_table.jsonl
research/team_game_special_teams_table.jsonl

# Preseason Engine Freeze sprint (2026-08-30): five more derived per-
# game/per-player corpora (3-7MB each) found during this same audit,
# structurally identical in kind to the already-ignored
# research/player_sog/player_game_sog.jsonl and siblings above (a
# pre-existing inconsistency this freeze corrects, not new policy) --
# all reproducible via their own real build scripts.
research/goalie_saves/goalie_game_saves.jsonl
research/goalie_saves/team_game_sog.jsonl
research/team_sog/team_game_sog.jsonl
research/team_goals_period/team_game_period_goals.jsonl
research/goalie_intelligence/actual_starters.jsonl
research/goalie_intelligence/goalie_appearances.jsonl
